I disagreed with Cyde all through this set of posts, but this is one area 
where I do agree with him -- I don't give a fig about my score. If I did, 
I'd try to carry as many artifacts with me, pudding farm, and do all the 
other things to jack my score up as high as possible. But I don't care 
about score. Having a ten million, or hundred billion*, score makes no 
difference in an ascension or how the game treats an ascension, or a 
death.

If I die with 10,000,000 points, it's still a death, even if my ascension 
is at 9,999,999 points. Nethack isn't Pac-Man or some other game where the 
only real victory is having your initials on a score chart. I consider 
myself a good player, despite having only ascended twice (and both were 
valkyries). I play for fun, and the score system doesn't strike me as fun 
in nethack.

* All score figures made up off the top of my head, obviously, so if 
they're not possible, oh well.


